---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import {
  APP_NAME,
  BUSINESS_NAME,
  SUPPORT_EMAIL,
} from 'astro:env/client';

const effectiveDate = 'April 20, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title={`Privacy | ${APP_NAME}`}
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data. Anonymous analytics via TelemetryDeck, nothing else.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="doc__meta">Effective: {effectiveDate}.</p>
  </header>

  <p>
    This policy covers {APP_NAME}, an async iMessage game
    published by {BUSINESS_NAME}. The game has no server of its
    own. Drawings and gameplay state are encoded into the iMessage URL
    and travel directly between players, so we cannot see, store, or
    access them. In-app purchases are processed by Apple. The only
    signal that reaches us is the anonymous app analytics described
    below.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We use TelemetryDeck to analyze app usage under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR
      legitimate interest, as we require reliable and efficient tools
      for collecting app usage data.
    </p>
    <p>Data transferred:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>An anonymized, untraceable user ID (per app installation).</li>
      <li>Actions defined by the app publisher (for example, "app launched," "settings opened").</li>
      <li>Rounded timestamps (nearest hour).</li>
      <li>Device metadata (system and app version, device type).</li>
      <li>Publisher-defined metadata.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Data not collected:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>No IP addresses (not in logs, not in the database).</li>
      <li>No cookies or tracking technologies.</li>
      <li>No persistent identifiers that could be traced back to individuals.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We use these signals to understand which features are used, detect
      bugs, and improve the app. We do not run advertising, we do not
      build user profiles, and we do not sell data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Drawings and reporting</h2>
    <p>
      Drawings are shared only with the players you send them to. They
      travel inside the iMessage URL and never pass through our systems
      because we do not operate any. To flag a prompt word as offensive
      or inappropriate, tap Report on the word inside the app to send
      us an email, and we will look at it when we can. To stop
      receiving messages from a specific player, use iMessage's block
      feature.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      We do not collect or store payment information. In-app purchases
      are processed by Apple under <SiteLink
        href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/"
        target="_blank"
        aria-label="Apple's privacy policy, opens in new tab"
      >Apple's privacy policy</SiteLink>&#8288;.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics are processed by TelemetryDeck GmbH, Von-der-Tann-Str.
      54, 86159 Augsburg, Germany. See their policy at
      <SiteLink
        href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy"
        target="_blank"
        aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab"
      >telemetrydeck.com/privacy</SiteLink>&#8288;. We require TelemetryDeck to
      protect your data at the same standard described in this policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      The analytics data above is anonymous, so there is no personal
      record attached to you to retain or delete. You can disable
      collection entirely from the Analytics setting inside the app.
      After you turn it off, no further signals are sent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your GDPR rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, correct, or object to the processing
      of personal data that relates to you. Because the analytics
      described above are anonymous and cannot be traced back to an
      individual, we cannot associate a request with a specific user.
      Where no personal record exists, we will tell you that.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>This app does not track your online activities across third-party websites or services.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} is not directed at children under 13 and does
      not knowingly collect personal information from them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      When we make a material change, we bump the effective date at the
      top of this page and surface a notice inside the app before the
      change takes effect.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Data controller: {BUSINESS_NAME}. Questions about this
      policy: <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink>&#8288;.
    </p>
  </section>
</Doc>
